<article class="env-lemma" id="01SD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01SD">Lemma <span data-tag="01SD">29.11.9</span>.</a> The base change of an affine morphism is affine. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $f : X \to S$ be an affine morphism. Let $S' \to S$ be any morphism. Denote $f' : X_{S'} = S' \times _ S X \to S'$ the base change of $f$. For every $s' \in S'$ there exists an open affine neighbourhood $s' \in V \subset S'$ which maps into some open affine $U \subset S$. By assumption $f^{-1}(U)$ is affine. By the material in Schemes, Section <a href="/tag/01JO" data-tag="01JO">26.17</a> we see that $f^{-1}(U)_ V = V \times _ U f^{-1}(U)$ is affine and equal to $(f')^{-1}(V)$. This proves that $S'$ has an open covering by affines whose inverse image under $f'$ is affine. We conclude by Lemma <a href="/tag/01S8" data-tag="01S8">29.11.3</a> above. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>